    "captureApi": "FViewport::TakeHighResScreenShot with FHighResScreenshotConfig (Engine/Public/UnrealClient.h, Engine/Public/HighResScreenshot.h) at run time in the game; unreal.AutomationLibrary.take_high_res_screenshot in this editor script, which is the editor-side wrapper over the same path.",
    "packagedSupport": "Yes. Both FViewport::TakeHighResScreenShot and GetHighResScreenshotConfig are plain ENGINE_API in 5.8 with no WITH_EDITOR and no !UE_BUILD_SHIPPING guard, and the file is written through the engine's image write queue, which ships. Setting FilenameOverride to an absolute path makes FScreenshotRequest skip its numbered-suffix logic and write exactly that PNG. What this editor script proves is that the path produces a correct file; it does not itself run in a packaged build.",
    "limitations": [
      "Numeric only. A PNG that is the right size and not blank is not a good photograph; nobody has looked at these.",
      "The editor viewport is not the game viewport. This proves the engine's high resolution path writes a correct file on this machine; it does not prove the packaged Shipping build does, only that the API it uses carries no editor-only or non-shipping guard.",
      "Depth of field, colour grades and exposure compensation are applied by the C++ on the photo camera's own post process settings and are not exercised here at all.",
      "The leash battery is arithmetic against the same clamp order the C++ uses. It says nothing about level collision: photo mode deliberately flies through walls, it only refuses to leave the world."
    ]
  },
